            "title_color": "#14151A"
          },
          "elements": []
        },
        {
          "id": "11e",
          "elType": "widget",
          "widgetType": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "tabs": [
              {
                "tab_title": "Task 1 &mdash; Reproduce the Bug",
                "tab_content": "Run the current report (starter/naive_report.py, provided as-is) and compare its row count to the number of distinct orders. Then check its reported status for O-2008 against what the payments team confirms (refunded, not paid).",
                "_id": "11f"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Task 2 &mdash; Find Where the Extra Rows Come From",
                "tab_content": "Look at order_events.csv grouped by order_id. Most orders with more than one row went through legitimate status changes. One order, O-2003, has two byte-for-byte identical rows: the same delivery arriving twice.",
                "_id": "120"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Task 3 &mdash; Drop Exact Duplicate Deliveries",
                "tab_content": "Remove rows that exactly match another row already kept, and remember which order_id(s) had one dropped so you can surface a had_duplicate_delivery flag.",
                "_id": "121"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Task 4 &mdash; Pick the True Latest Event, Not the Last One in the File",
                "tab_content": "The true latest event is the one with the greatest event_ts, except a few rows are missing event_ts entirely and a few tie on event_ts exactly. Use sequence_no as the tie-break.",
                "_id": "122"
              },
              {
                "tab_title": "Task 5 &mdash; Assemble and Verify",
                "tab_content": "Combine Tasks 3-4 into starter/dedupe.py so it returns exactly one row per order_id. Then run python tests/test_solution.py &mdash; it exits non-zero if any check fails.",
                "_id": "123"
              }
            ],
            "title_color": "#14151A",
            "content_color": "#54575F",
            "border_color": "#E7E3D9",
            "faq_schema": "no"
          },
          "elements": []
        }
      ]
    },
